==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/vwa.la/|lang=fr}}, {{SAMPA|/vwa.la/}}

===Etymology===
From ''vois là'', 'look there'.

===Verb===
# [[there|There]] is.
#: ''Voilà l’homme tout entier, s’en prenant à sa chaussure alors que c’est son pied le coupable.'' — Beckett, Samuel
#::''There is man in his entirety, blaming his shoe when his foot is guilty.'' — Beckett, Samuel
# [[here|Here]] is.
#: ''Voilà le fromage''
#:: ''Here's the cheese''
#[[that|That]] is.
#:''Voilà ce que je lui ai demandé, et voici sa réponse : « ... »''
#::''That's what I asked her and this is her answer: "..."''

===Usage Notes===
#''voilà'' is a [[defective]] verb. Its only conjugation is at the present indicative tense even if it can appear in phrases in another tense.
#it is mainly used to introduce slightly distant person or object, in opposition to ''[[voici]]'' used to designate person or object near the speaker.
#in face to face conversations where both contributors can see the subject of the conversation, ''voilà'' often supersede ''voici'' (thus its second definition: ''Here is'')

